// The Celestial Writing.
//
// From the wing's research file celestial.verified.json, with the points its
// fact-check left open taken from the later checks against the prints: the
// 1533 caption, page, signature and table layout, and the Latin of III.30,
// from the-books.verified.json (Library of Congress copy, page images; McGill
// copy, OCR); the II.51 and III.30 passages and their 1651 pages from
// agrippa.verified.json. Every English quotation is J.F.'s (London, 1651), as
// keyed in EEBO-TCP A26565 (CC0) and checked there.
//
// The signs are traced from the table of 1533 in the Library of Congress copy
// (loc.gov 0277, the plate agrippa-angelic-1533-loc-celestial), checked sign
// by sign against the McGill and Jung copies and compared with two copies of
// the English of 1651 (traced/celestial/glyphs.json, independently checked).
// Each glyph is the traced path data unchanged, so the page draws it exactly
// as the tracer's specimen sheet does. A letter's note carries only what the
// tracing tells a reader about that letter: a printed defect settled from
// another copy, a departure of the drawing, a variant of 1651 worth knowing.
// The plate is the same page of the Library of Congress copy, whose
// repository states no known restriction.
